{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     training.hbs — the /training/ landing page.
     Ported from NS-Design-System/templates/training-index.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     EVERY WORD AND EVERY MODULE ON THIS PAGE COMES FROM GHOST. There is no
     curriculum data in this theme and there must not be: modules and lessons
     are POSTS, written in Admin, and the whole point of the model in
     abstract/01-content-model.md is that adding one is Ghost-Admin-only work.

     ⚠ An earlier version of this file shipped the curriculum as JSON in
     assets/data/ and compiled it into generated templates at build time. That
     was wrong in the way that matters: it put content in the repo, so adding
     a lesson meant a commit and a deploy. It is recorded here only so nobody
     reinvents it.

     ── WHAT BACKS THIS PAGE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Nothing, directly — there is ONE training, so it has no post of its own.
     A Ghost PAGE with slug `training` supplies the title and lede if one
     exists; without it the page falls back to its own copy below, so the URL
     works on a fresh install.

     The MODULES are discovered: posts tagged #training-module, ordered
     published_at asc. Backdate a module post to move it earlier.

     ── THE BAND ORDER IS UPSTREAM'S, AND IT IS AN ARGUMENT ──────────────────
     NS-Design-System/templates/training-index.html sequences the page so it
     answers, in order:

       01 thero    what is this, and how do I search it
       02 sections what it will COVER          <- training/sections (copy)
       03 modules  what is written TODAY       <- training/modules  (GHOST)

     ⚠ THERE IS NO "FOUR STAGES" BAND, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. Upstream's §02
     is a .ns-path of four stages ("each ending where the next begins") and it
     was here. It went because it said the same thing as the Sections grid
     directly under it — six cards naming the same territory — so the page
     made its map twice, in two shapes, and the reader had to work out whether
     they were the same list. Sections survived because it is the one that
     pairs with the real modules below it. The band still exists as
     partials/home/path.hbs if it is ever wanted back.
       04 tiers    what does it cost           <- training/tiers   (copy)
       05 pace     how long will it take       <- training/pace    (copy)
       06 people   who maintains it            <- training/people  (GHOST)
       07 cta      the one closer              <- home/cta

     Upstream's §03 is a grid of static track cards. Here that slot is the
     REAL curriculum from Ghost, which is the one deliberate divergence: a
     hand-written grid of tracks would be the same content-in-the-theme
     mistake the modules band exists to avoid.

     ── WHICH BANDS MAY HOLD COPY, AND WHICH MAY NOT ─────────────────────────
     path, tiers and pace are MARKETING bands - editorial claims about how the
     material is organised, what it costs and how long it takes, exactly like
     every partial in partials/home/. They carry copy and are marked DUMMY.

     modules and people are CONTENT and come from Ghost. Nothing about the
     curriculum or the authors is ever written into a template. If you are
     about to type a module name into a .hbs file, that is the line.

     ── `hash-training-module`, NOT `#training-module` ───────────────────────
     In a FILTER STRING Ghost writes an internal tag with a `hash-` prefix.
     `tag:#training-module` matches nothing, silently, and an empty curriculum
     looks exactly like a curriculum that has not been written yet.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

<section class="ns-thero">
    <div class="ns-thero__inner">
        <div class="ns-thero__body">
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Training"}}</span>

            {{!-- The page fork. {{#page}} only has a body if a Ghost page with
                 this slug exists; the {{else}} is what keeps /training/
                 working before anyone has made one. --}}
            {{#page}}
                <h1 class="ns-thero__title">{{title}}</h1>
                {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-thero__lede">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
            {{else}}
                <h1 class="ns-thero__title">{{t "Every Salesforce skill, in the order you need it"}}</h1>
                <p class="ns-thero__lede">{{t "Written training you read at your own pace and search when you just need the answer."}}</p>
            {{/page}}

            {{!-- ── ACTIONS AND STATS ARE PART OF .ns-thero ────────────────
                 demo-training-index.html's hero is kicker / title / lede /
                 ACTIONS / search / STATS. Shipping only the first three and
                 the search left the hero looking like a search page rather
                 than a landing page — that is the "not the same" gap.

                 "Start at the beginning" points at the FIRST lesson of the
                 FIRST module, found by publish order, so it keeps working
                 when modules are reordered or the first one is replaced. If
                 nothing is published the button is not drawn at all, because
                 a primary action that leads nowhere is worse than none. --}}
            <div class="ns-thero__actions">
                {{#get "posts" filter="tag:[hash-training-lesson,hash-training-content]" order="published_at asc" limit="1" as |first|}}
                    {{#foreach first}}
                        <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary ns-btn--lg" href="{{url}}">{{> "icons/rocket-launch"}} {{t "Start at the beginning"}}</a>
                    {{/foreach}}
                {{/get}}
                <a class="ns-btn" href="#modules">{{t "Browse the curriculum"}}</a>
            </div>

            <form class="ns-thero__search" role="search" data-ghost-search>
                <div class="ns-input-wrap">
                    <span class="ns-input-wrap__icon">{{> "icons/magnifying-glass"}}</span>
                    {{!-- ⚠ .ns-input--has-icon is NOT optional beside
                         .ns-input-wrap__icon: the icon is absolutely
                         positioned and pushes nothing, so this modifier is the
                         padding that stops the placeholder rendering
                         underneath it. Upstream's own training-index.html
                         omits it and shows the overlap. --}}
                    <input class="ns-input ns-input--has-icon" type="search" name="q"
                           placeholder="{{t "Search the training"}}"
                           aria-label="{{t "Search the training"}}">
                </div>
            </form>
            {{!-- ⚠ EVERY FIGURE IS COUNTED, NEVER TYPED. {{#get}} exposes
                 {{pagination.total}}, which is the real number of matching
                 posts — a hand-written stat is one that stops being true the
                 first time something is published and nothing catches it.
                 "Free" is the one literal, and it is a policy rather than a
                 count. --}}
            <div class="ns-thero__stats">
                {{#get "posts" filter="tag:[hash-training-module,hash-training-section]" limit="1"}}<span><b>{{pagination.total}}</b>{{t "Modules"}}</span>{{/get}}
                {{#get "posts" filter="tag:[hash-training-lesson,hash-training-content]" limit="1"}}<span><b>{{pagination.total}}</b>{{t "Lessons"}}</span>{{/get}}
                {{#get "tags" filter="visibility:public" limit="1"}}<span><b>{{pagination.total}}</b>{{t "Topics"}}</span>{{/get}}
                <span><b>{{t "Free"}}</b>{{t "Everything"}}</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ns-thero__art" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="ns-tthumb ns-tthumb--glyph">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}}</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

